  "question": {
    "text": "A particle moves towards east from a point $A$ to a point $B$ at the rate of $4 \\mathrm{~km} / \\mathrm{h}$ and then towards north from $B$ to $C$ at the rate of $5 \\mathrm{~km} / \\mathrm{h}$. If $A B=12 \\mathrm{~km}$ and $B C=5 \\mathrm{~km}$, then its average speed for its journey from $A$ to $C$ and resultant average velocity direct from $A$ to $C$ are respectively",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "9fiby",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{17}{4} \\mathrm{~km} / \\mathrm{h}$ and $\\frac{13}{4} \\mathrm{~km} / \\mathrm{h}$\n",
